	Narrator: Simon is standing beside an old tree, looking at whatever is on the ground. Catherine approaches slowly until Simon notices her.
	[wait time="1.0"]
	join Simon (Simon_normal) center
	Simon (Simon_surprised): Oh, I didn’t see you there. Are you leaving Shateroo? You look like someone is preparing to leave.
	catherine: I don’t know. I don’t know anything anymore.
Simon (Simon_talking): I hope you have found what you came for.
catherine: I found it but it wasn't enough. I wish I had more time to figure things out.
- Ask Simon whether wanting more is selfish
	catherine: Is it selfish to want more time? Even when you know you cannot have it?
	Simon: I don’t think so, wanting something is not a crime.
	catherine: What if someone gets hurt because you want it?
	Simon: Then the wanting is innocent. What you do for it is another matter.
	leave Simon
	set {ChapterTracking.is_evil} = false
	set {EndingTracking.catherine_sympathy} += 1.0
- Ask Simon whether Catherine should accept fate
	catherine: Perhaps I should simply accept that this is how things end.
	Simon: Sometimes we don’t really have a choice, you know, look at me. Do you think I want to be a grave polisher? But acceptance is not always surrender.
	catherine: Stop with your philosophical speech. What's the difference anyway?
	Simon: Let’s put it like this. Acceptance says, "This is what happened." Surrender says, "There was never anything worth fighting for."
	catherine: And which one do you think I'm doing?
	Simon: What I say here doesn’t really matter. That’s up to you to decide.
	leave Simon
	set {ChapterTracking.is_evil} = true
	set {EndingTracking.catherine_sympathy} -= 1.0
